\ Smoke test for the module cache lock: task-context readers hammer the
\ cache-hit path of `load`, and the main task inserts fresh modules into the
\ cache around them.
\
\ Two pre-existing defects constrain its shape. Task execution overlapping a
\ main-task load reads the load's transient import frame and crashes, so the
\ main task does not load while the readers run, and the file runs under
\ --threads=1. A task executing a scope-local word poisons the next load, so
\ the reader body is inlined into each spawn instead. Widen this to
\ overlapping cross-worker coverage once both are fixed.

use "testing" ;

"cache-hit readers from task contexts" test-section

\ Prime the readers' module so every load in the tasks below is a hit.
"./task_load_cache_readers_hit_mod.1z" load drop

[
  done: 3 <buffered-channel> ;
  [
    100 [
      "./task_load_cache_readers_hit_mod.1z" load
      hit-mod-word: @get call drop
    ] times
    t done send
  ] spawn drop
  [
    100 [
      "./task_load_cache_readers_hit_mod.1z" load
      hit-mod-word: @get call drop
    ] times
    t done send
  ] spawn drop
  [
    100 [
      "./task_load_cache_readers_hit_mod.1z" load
      hit-mod-word: @get call drop
    ] times
    t done send
  ] spawn drop
  done receive drop
  done receive drop
  done receive drop
] task-scope

"cache inserts after task readers" test-section

{ "math" "strings" "char" "bytes" "sets" "ranges" } [ load drop ] #each

"./task_load_cache_readers_hit_mod.1z" load
hit-mod-word: @get call "hit" "the hit module still works after the reader storm" assert=
